\section{Performance metric calculations}{

The \code{\link[=evalmod]{evalmod()}} function calculates ROC and Precision-Recall
curves and returns an \code{S3} object. The generated \code{S3} object can
be used with several different \code{S3} generics, such as \code{print} and
\code{\link[=plot]{plot()}}. The \code{\link[=evalmod]{evalmod()}} function can also
calculate basic evaluation metrics - error rate, accuracy, specificity,
sensitivity, precision, Matthews correlation coefficient, F-score,
balanced accuracy, negative predictive value, informedness, markedness,
and Cohen's kappa.
}

\section{Data preparation}{

The \code{\link[=mmdata]{mmdata()}} function creates an input dataset for
the \code{\link[=evalmod]{evalmod()}} function. The generated dataset contains
formatted scores and labels.

\code{\link[=join_scores]{join_scores()}} and \code{\link[=join_labels]{join_labels()}} are helper
functions to combine multiple scores and labels.

The \code{\link[=create_sim_samples]{create_sim_samples()}} function creates test datasets with
five different performance levels.
}

\section{Data visualization}{

\code{\link[=plot]{plot()}} takes an \code{S3} object generated
by \code{\link[=evalmod]{evalmod()}} as input and plot corresponding curves.

\code{\link[=autoplot]{autoplot()}} uses \code{ggplot} to plot curves.
}

\section{Result retrieval}{

\code{\link[=as.data.frame]{as.data.frame()}} takes an \code{S3} object generated
by \code{\link[=evalmod]{evalmod()}} as input and and returns a data frame
with calculated curve points.

\code{\link[=auc]{auc()}} and \code{\link[=pauc]{pauc()}} returns a data frame with AUC scores
and partial AUC scores, respectively. \code{\link[=auc_ci]{auc_ci()}}
returns confidence intervals of AUCs for both ROC
and precision-recall curves.

\code{\link[=average_precision]{average_precision()}} returns the step estimator of the area under the
precision-recall curve, and \code{\link[=prbe]{prbe()}} the precision-recall break-even
point.
}

\section{Probability-based metrics}{

\code{\link[=prob_metrics]{prob_metrics()}} calculates the Brier score and the log loss of
prediction scores that are probabilities, and \code{\link[=prob_metrics_ci]{prob_metrics_ci()}}
returns their confidence intervals over multiple test datasets.
}

\section{Uncertainty from one test set}{

\code{\link[=auc_boot]{auc_boot()}} resamples a single test set so that \code{\link[=auc_ci]{auc_ci()}} can put a
percentile interval around its AUC, and \code{\link[=auc_diff]{auc_diff()}} can compare two
models on the same resamples.
}

\section{Classification report}{

\code{\link[=classification_report]{classification_report()}} reports precision, recall and the F-score of
every class at one operating point, in the layout \code{scikit-learn}'s
function of that name prints.
}

